 "intro_zh": "亚兹德市位于伊朗高原中部，距伊斯法罕东南270公里，紧邻香料之路和丝绸之路。它是利用有限资源在沙漠中生存的活生生的见证。通过坎儿井系统向城市供水，该系统是为了抽取地下水而开发的。亚兹德的土建筑逃脱了摧毁许多传统土城镇的现代化进程，保留了其传统地区、坎儿井系统、传统房屋、集市、土耳其浴室、清真寺、犹太教堂、琐罗亚斯德教寺庙和历史悠久的多拉特阿巴德花园。",
 "intro_zh_source": "machine_translation",
 "intro_en": "The City of Yazd is located in the middle of the Iranian plateau, 270 km southeast of Isfahan, close to the Spice and Silk Roads. It bears living testimony to the use of limited resources for survival in the desert. Water is supplied to the city through a qanat system developed to draw underground water. The earthen architecture of Yazd has escaped the modernization that destroyed many traditional earthen towns, retaining its traditional districts, the qanat system, traditional houses, bazars, hammams, mosques, synagogues, Zoroastrian temples and the historic garden of Dolat-abad.",
 "intro_en_source": "unesco_official",
